===Etymology===
1890, from {{etyl|de|en}} {{term|Wurst||sausage, wurst|lang=de}} from {{etyl|gmh|en}} {{term|wurst|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|en}} {{term|wurst|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*wurstiz||something turned or twisted}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*wert-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*-d-||to turn}}. Akin to {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|worst||wurst|lang=osx}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|weorþan||to turn, become|lang=ang}}. Unrelated to {{term|worsted||type of yarn|lang=en}}. More at {{m|en|worth||to be, become, betide}}.

